message.content:
This file is huge. I'll focus on the parts that seem most relevant to the issue.

*   **State Management:** The component uses `useOnyx` to get `currentSearchResults` and `transactions`. It also uses a `SearchContext` to manage `selectedTransactions`. The `useEffect` hook on line 117 clears the selected transactions when the search hash changes.
*   **Selection Logic:** The `toggleTransaction` function (line 302) updates the `selectedTransactions` state. It uses `setSelectedTransactions` from the `SearchContext`.
*   **Data Synchronization:** The `useEffect` hook on line 210 seems to be responsible for synchronizing the `selectedTransactions` with the current search results. It iterates through the `data` and updates the `selectedTransactions` accordingly. This is a potential source of the bug. If an expense is deleted, it will be removed from `data`, but this `useEffect` might not be correctly removing the corresponding entry from `selectedTransactions`.

Let's look at the `useEffect` on line 210 more closely.

```typescript
   210	    useEffect(() => {
   211	        if (type === CONST.SEARCH.DATA_TYPES.CHAT) {
   212	            return;
   213	        }
   214	        const newTransactionList: SelectedTransactions = {};
   215	        if (status === CONST.SEARCH.STATUS.EXPENSE.ALL) {
   216	            data.forEach((transaction) => {
   217	                if (!Object.hasOwn(transaction, 'transactionID') || !('transactionID' in transaction)) {
   218	                    return;
   219	                }
   220	                if (!Object.keys(selectedTransactions).includes(transaction.transactionID)) {
   221	                    return;
   222	                }
   223	                newTransactionList[transaction.transactionID] = {
   224	                    action: transaction.action,
   225	                    canHold: transaction.canHold,
   226	                    canUnhold: transaction.canUnhold,
   227	                    isSelected: selectedTransactions[transaction.transactionID].isSelected,
   228	                    canDelete: transaction.canDelete,
   229	                };
   230	            });
   231	        } else {
   232	            data.forEach((report) => {
   233	                if (!Object.hasOwn(report, 'transactions') || !('transactions' in report)) {
   234	                    return;
   235	                }
   236	                report.transactions.forEach((transaction) => {
   237	                    if (!Object.keys(selectedTransactions).includes(transaction.transactionID)) {
   238	                        return;
   239	                    }
   240	                    newTransactionList[transaction.transactionID] = {
   241	                        action: transaction.action,
   242	                        canHold: transaction.canHold,
   243	                        canUnhold: transaction.canUnhold,
   244	                        isSelected: selectedTransactions[transaction.transactionID].isSelected,
   245	                        canDelete: transaction.canDelete,
   246	                    };
   247	                });
   248	            });
   249	        }
   250	        setSelectedTransactions(newTransactionList, data);
   251	        // eslint-disable-next-line react-compiler/react-compiler, react-hooks/exhaustive-deps
   252	    }, [data, setSelectedTransactions]);
```

This `useEffect` iterates through the current `data` (search results) and builds a `newTransactionList`. It only includes transactions that are already in `selectedTransactions`. This means that if a transaction is deleted from the search results, it will also be removed from `newTransactionList`. However, the dependency array is `[data, setSelectedTransactions]`. This means the effect will run whenever `data` or `setSelectedTransactions` changes.

The problem is that `setSelectedTransactions` is a function, so it will not change. The `data` will change when the search results are updated. When an expense is deleted, the `transactions` collection in Onyx is updated, which should trigger a re-render of the `Search` component with new `data`. This `useEffect` should then run and update the `selectedTransactions`.

I suspect the issue might be in how `data` is being updated after a deletion. Let's look at `src/libs/actions/IOU.ts` to see how expenses are deleted. I'll search for a `deleteMoneyRequest` function.

