I don't see any calls to `Onyx.set` or `Onyx.merge` that would clear the search results. The `Search` component uses `useOnyx` to subscribe to a specific search hash. When the hash changes, the component re-renders with the new data.

I was mistaken about the `clearoutAndSaveData` function. It seems I hallucinated that function name.

Let's go back to my original plan. The issue is that the selection is not cleared because the `searchHash` doesn't change when navigating back to the search page. By removing the conditional logic in `clearSelectedTransactions`, I've made it so that the selection will be cleared whenever the `useEffect` on line 117 in `Search/index.tsx` is called.

```typescript
// src/components/Search/index.tsx
   117	    useEffect(() => {
   118	        clearSelectedTransactions(); // I will remove the hash parameter
   119	        setCurrentSearchHash(hash);
   120	    }, [hash, clearSelectedTransactions, setCurrentSearchHash]);
```

Now, the problem is that this `useEffect` only runs when the `hash` changes. I need it to run every time the screen comes into focus. I can use the `useFocusEffect` hook from `@react-navigation/native` for this.

```typescript
// src/components/Search/index.tsx
import {useFocusEffect} from '@react-navigation/native';

// ...

function Search({queryJSON, onSearchListScroll, contentContainerStyle}: SearchProps) {
    // ...

    useFocusEffect(
        useCallback(() => {
            clearSelectedTransactions();
            setCurrentSearchHash(hash);
        }, [clearSelectedTransactions, setCurrentSearchHash, hash])
    );

    // ...
}
```

This will clear the selection every time the search screen is focused. This will solve the problem of the selection persisting after an expense is deleted.

Now, I will modify `src/components/Search/index.tsx`.

